{%- doc -%}
  Outputs the price a selling plan allocation shows on the PDP, in cents. A value, not markup,
  so a caller can capture it and format it however it already formats prices:

    {%- capture sub_price -%}
      {%- render 'selling-plan-display-price', allocation: variant.selling_plan_allocations.first -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}

  Shopify rounds a percentage selling plan to the nearest cent (25% off $9.99 is $7.49), while
  the automatic discount price beside it is rounded up (auto-discount-price-value.liquid shows
  $7.50). Recomputing the plan price the same way keeps the two rows agreeing. Display only:
  checkout still charges allocation.price.

  @param {selling_plan_allocation} allocation - The allocation to price
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign base = allocation.compare_at_price | default: allocation.price
  assign adjustment = allocation.selling_plan.price_adjustments.first
  assign display_price = allocation.price

  if adjustment.value_type == 'percentage' and base > 0
    assign remaining = 100.0 | minus: adjustment.value
    # round: 4 first, so float noise (749.0000001) is not pushed up a whole cent.
    assign display_price = base | times: remaining | divided_by: 100.0 | round: 4 | ceil
  endif

  echo display_price
-%}
